extern fn void WorldId.set_user_data(self, void* user_data) @cname("b3World_SetUserData");

<*
 Replaces the world's friction mixing with fcn, and restores box3d's own when fcn is null. A
 locked world — mid step(), or inside a callback it runs — keeps the mixing it has, under an
 assertion this build compiles out. See FrictionFn for what box3d then calls, and how often.
*>
extern fn void WorldId.set_friction_callback(self, FrictionFn fcn) @cname("b3World_SetFrictionCallback");

<*
 Replaces the world's restitution mixing with fcn, and restores box3d's own when fcn is null. A
 locked world keeps the mixing it has, under the same assertion this build compiles out. See
 RestitutionFn for what box3d then calls, and how often.
*>
extern fn void WorldId.set_restitution_callback(self, RestitutionFn fcn) @cname("b3World_SetRestitutionCallback");

extern fn void WorldId.rebuild_static_tree(self) @cname("b3World_RebuildStaticTree");

<*
 An explosion definition. The impulse fades to nothing across falloff, which reaches beyond radius,
 and impulse_per_area scales with the area of each shape facing the blast; it may be negative,
 which pulls inward instead of pushing out.
*>
struct ExplosionDef {
    ulong mask_bits;
    Pos position;
    float radius;
    float falloff;
    float impulse_per_area;
}

<*
 Raw explosion. Private because WorldId.explode() refuses the definitions box3d does no more than
 assert against, this release build compiling those assertions out.
*>
extern fn void world_explode_raw(WorldId world_id, ExplosionDef* def) @cname("b3World_Explode") @private;

<*
 An explosion definition that moves nothing: every mask bit set, the position at the origin, and
 radius, falloff and impulse_per_area all zero. Every field but the mask has to be filled in, and
 an unfilled one is accepted and silently does nothing where an incomplete joint def is refused.
*>
extern fn ExplosionDef default_explosion_def() @cname("b3DefaultExplosionDef");

